/-!
# Characteristic-two Sylow automorphism fixers for B.1.13

The full model interface includes every characteristic-two classical and
exceptional family, with actual equivalences and exact small-derived cases.
The proved branches are PSL₂, PSL₃, nonbinary PSp₄, Suzuki, G₂ (including
G₂(2)′), PSp₄(2)′, and the Tits endpoint. Each supplies the actual conjugation-action
containment argument through the perfect component's central quotient.

The remaining classical ranks, unitary groups, exceptional F/E families,
triality and large Ree still require their
intrinsic model proofs. This module does not assert the general family
theorem until those obligations have been discharged.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, B.1.13, printed pp.73–74 (PDF pp.84–85).
-/
